# Ending — The Regular Pioneer (BACKLOG § Endings, "the doubling-down
# ending"). Quiet, settled, slightly weary. The player got what they were
# taught to want; everything outside the org quietly receded.
# TODO: authenticity check — ending draft.

Five years later.
You've been a regular pioneer for four of them. You know every street in the territory by its dogs.
Brother Phillips stepped down as coordinator last spring. At his last meeting in the role he put a hand on your shoulder and didn't say anything, which you understood.
if GameState.flag("activity_coworker_invite") > 0:
	Dana from work got married. The invitation is still on your fridge. It was a nice card.
else:
	The people from your old job text less now. Then not at all. You didn't notice when.
Some mornings, before the car group, you sit in the driveway with the engine off and the heater running. You don't pray, exactly. You just sit.
Then you go. You always go.
